%%{init: {"sequence": {"wrap": true, "width": 210, "noteMargin": 8}}}%%
%% Reserve: the first step of checkout. Browser -> api -> Redis fd_reserve -> Postgres, with idempotency handling.
%% Source of docs/diagrams/reserve-checkout.svg. Checkout submit is in checkout-submit.mmd.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor B as Browser
  participant A as api
  participant R as Redis fd_reserve
  participant P as Postgres

  Note over B,A: Buy pressed. Idempotency-Key K created once per buy intent, kept in sessionStorage per drop
  B->>A: POST /api/v1/drops/:dropId/reservations, Idempotency-Key K, body qty
  Note over A,R: rid = uuidv5(user:drop:K), fp = sha256(body). PG breaker open → 503 before Redis
  A->>R: FCALL fd_reserve rid uid qty fp
  alt drop RECONCILING
    R-->>A: RETRY
    A-->>B: 503 Retry-After 1, same key
  else drop not in Redis
    R-->>A: NO_DROP
    A-->>B: replay if the order exists in PG · else 503 + rebuild nudge if the drop is tracked · else 409 DROP_NOT_LIVE
  else NOT_LIVE, LIMIT or SOLD_OUT
    R-->>A: rejection, read-only path, no writes
    A-->>B: 409 DROP_NOT_LIVE, LIMIT_REACHED or SOLD_OUT
  else rid already in rsv
    R-->>A: EXISTING with state and gen, or FP_MISMATCH
    opt FP_MISMATCH
      A-->>B: 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
    end
  else admitted
    Note over R,P: avail - q, held + q, uq + q, rsv HELD, ZADD exp, seq + 1, PUBLISH fd:ch:stock:{d:dropId}
    R-->>A: RESERVED with gen
  end
  Note over A,P: Only RESERVED or EXISTING continue. Postgres now decides the reservation's fate

  A->>P: BEGIN, INSERT orders id=rid status RESERVED ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  alt row already exists - duplicate or concurrent retry
    P-->>A: 0 rows
    A->>P: ROLLBACK, SELECT order rid
    A-->>B: 200 replay (current order) · 409 if REJECTED · 410 if expired · 422 if request_hash differs
  else new order
    A->>P: UPSERT user_drop_quota WHERE claimed + q within limit_qty
    alt limit exceeded - Redis uq was optimistic
      A->>P: ROLLBACK, then tombstone REJECTED LIMIT
      A-->>B: 409 LIMIT_REACHED (or the concurrent winner's order), reconciler nudged
    else quota claimed
      A->>P: INSERT outbox order.reserved
      A->>P: UPDATE drop_inventory hot row LAST, guarded by redis_gen, stock and the drop window
      alt all guards pass
        A->>P: COMMIT
        A-->>B: 201 orderId=rid, expiresAt, serverNow
      else stale redis_gen - a rebuild happened
        A->>P: ROLLBACK
        A-->>B: 503 Retry-After 1, retry with the same key
      else SOLD_OUT or NOT_LIVE
        A->>P: ROLLBACK, then tombstone REJECTED SOLD_OUT or NOT_LIVE
        A-->>B: 409, settlement later releases the Redis hold
      end
    end
  end
  Note over A,P: Tombstone = one statement: INSERT REJECTED ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING feeds the outbox INSERT, so order.rejected exists only if the tombstone won
